Pi-hole FTL (Faster Than Light) is the engine of the Pi-hole network-wide
ad blocker: a DNS and DHCP server built on dnsmasq that answers queries for
blocked domains itself, keeps statistics and a query log in SQLite, and
serves the Pi-hole API and web interface through its embedded web server.

This is the native FreeBSD build of FTL, from the FreedomNAS fork that
carries the FreeBSD support.
